      "decision": "DEFER_FULL_MULTICASE_CONTRACT_BRIDGE",
      "reason": "The methods name the same broad notation-family rival, and slash versus or alone is not a distinction. However, GDT215 explicitly targets q13 and develops its comparison against long practical medical records and diagram-local reference; GDT008 compares manuscript-wide architectures, and GDT108 performs a later evidence-bounded revision. The three methods do not bind one fully specified unchanged notation-only rival across all three historical cases. Do not import the detailed selected hybrid generator into the notation-only alternative. Identical coarse wording is insufficient for whole-card equality; differing evidence panels alone also do not prove incompatible propositions.",
      "smallest_missing_bridge": "An explicit authored definition or declared unchanged rival contract that states the common notation-only generator and its domain across GDT008, GDT108 and the q13 GDT215 case. Until such material exists, reuse this defer receipt; no rerun or repeated same-source comparison.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "path": "GDT108_HPR2_COUPLED_ADDRESS_THEORY_METHOD.md",
          "line": 3,
          "line_end": 23,
          "quote": "## Purpose\n\nRevise the leading YOLO generative theory after GDT101--GDT107. This is\nabductive theory generation, not confirmation. It must choose a leading model,\nexplain the strongest positive and negative results together, and freeze\nnon-f84 predictions.\n\n## Inputs\n\nBind GDT003 and GDT100--GDT107. Archived external annotations remain\nhypothesis-generation evidence only. No threshold or effect is imported as\nfresh confirmation.\n\n## Compared theories\n\n1. compressed/abbreviated natural language;\n2. semantic/technical notation;\n3. hybrid content-address + abbreviation + record/relationship compiler.\n\nScore ten explicit abductive criteria at 0/1. The scores are transparent\ntheory bookkeeping, not probabilities.",
          "sha256": "f25fae61640758509501252af5f66ec2f6243986cd57ac3d5a7a3ad589139bde"
        },
        {
          "path": "GDT215_Q13_GENERATIVE_THEORY_METHOD.md",
          "line": 3,
          "line_end": 17,
          "quote": "## Purpose\n\nGDT215 selects the strongest current generative theory for the q13 biological/\nbalneological pages.  It is an abductive YOLO synthesis, not a confirmation\ntest and not a translation.  It compares three broad generators:\n\n1. compressed or abbreviated natural language;\n2. semantic or technical notation;\n3. a hybrid of language, abbreviation, record notation, and a diagram-local\n   reference register.\n\nThe third is required to win rather than leaving the three possibilities tied.\nIts provisional content prior is therapeutic balneology with an unusually\nschematic hydraulic or process rendering.  That prior is explicitly weaker\nthan the formal architecture.",
          "sha256": "09f77db5f065bd4d27d70e2d8685fd68f4d2c1a1d1fe47cc70c07f5ff2a489a8"
        },
        {
          "path": "GDT215_Q13_GENERATIVE_THEORY_METHOD.md",
          "line": 69,
          "line_end": 81,
          "quote": "Compressed natural language alone ranks third because authentic abbreviation\ncan generate part of the observed architecture, while the tested static\nlanguage decoders and stable global host dictionary do not explain the full\ncompiler, label/prose heterogeneity, or page-conditioned rebinding.\n\nTechnical notation alone remains live but ranks second because it naturally\nexplains opaque addresses and label registers, yet does not by itself explain\nthe long record-like prose or the readable medieval medical comparators.\n\nThe hybrid ranks first because it jointly accommodates the formal compiler,\npage-conditioned inventory, distinct label register, long practical records,\nfailed exact key dictionary, and external medical/balneological/hydraulic\ndocument precedents.  This is explanatory compression, not a fitted score.\n",
          "sha256": "09f77db5f065bd4d27d70e2d8685fd68f4d2c1a1d1fe47cc70c07f5ff2a489a8"
        },
        {
          "path": "GDT008_HYBRID_REGISTER_THEORY_METHOD.md",
          "line": 9,
          "line_end": 27,
          "quote": "## Purpose\n\nThis pass deliberately constructs the strongest concrete generative theory\ncompatible with the accumulated branch evidence. It is not a confirmation\ntest and does not require every component to be independently identifiable.\nPost-hoc synthesis and weak evidence are allowed, but every observation,\ninference, and speculative value must remain visibly distinct.\n\nThe three compared architectures are:\n\n1. compressed/abbreviated natural language;\n2. semantic or technical notation;\n3. a hybrid natural-language-derived technical register with abbreviation and\n   notation-like fields.\n\nThe selected architecture must explain the manuscript hierarchy, page and\nCurrier effects, line reset, productive formal reuse, split/join spellings,\nlabel compression, recurrent edge operations, repeated formulae, and the\nfailure of simple language/cipher mappings with one coherent generator.",
          "sha256": "f46828fa0afd7645d92017b5c2b8657901d3a564543697c50fab289bf1efa0cd"
        }
      ],
